meta {
  name: Settings
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Settings of the site: variables (texts, switches, templates, keys), themes of the storefront, site variations and information about the site. Run the requests in order:

  1. `Show site information` and `List site variations`: `code` of a variation is `site_variation` of other operations.
  2. `List rubrics of settings`, `List icons of settings`: the tree and icons that settings refer to.
  3. `List settings` (page by page, filters `rubric_id`, `codes`, `type`, `query`) and `Show a setting`; `Show the template context of settings` for `twig` settings (`twig_type`).
  4. `Save settings` then `Reset settings`: changes `is_show_out_of_stock_products` of the site and resets it to the default. Secrets come masked: a mask sent back is skipped. `mailer_host` is read-only (credentials of the mail server).
  5. Themes: `List themes` (`active` — the theme of the storefront, chosen by `default_theme`), `Create a theme` keeps `themeId`, then `Show`, `Update` and `Delete` it.
}
